<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Fade-in and Scale Animation</title>
</head>

<body>

  <div class="animation-placeholder"></div>

  <div class="animation-container">
    <img src="assets/images/Gemini generated logo svg from adobe.svg" alt="Your Image">
  </div>

  <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
  <p>This content will fade in smoothly. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nullam ut velit nec
    neque laoreet consectetur sit amet eu velit. Duis nec lacus tincidunt, venenatis ex eget, fermentum purus. Donec
    vehicula dui nec diam vulputate convallis. Nullam vehicula nunc at quam laoreet, non faucibus justo varius. Nam in
    quam vitae dui auctor interdum nec non metus. Integer vitae arcu id magna aliquam congue. Morbi et ipsum eget elit
    aliquam volutpat. Suspendisse sollicitudin hendrerit nulla id vehicula. Nam mattis tellus eu magna dapibus
    feugiat. Duis lacinia nec leo at tristique.</p>

  <script>
    // Wait for the DOM to be fully loaded
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
      // Get the image element
      var img = document.querySelector(".animation-container img");

      // Add the "show" class to trigger the animation after a delay
      setTimeout(function () {
        img.classList.add("show");
        img.style.animation = "reboundAnimation 2s ease-in-out forwards";
      }, 100); // Delay in milliseconds before starting the animation
    });
  </script>

</body>

</html>

